      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with a question: where is a derivative positive, and where is it negative? We'll come back to that. First, picture a hike. This curve is the trail's height as you walk along it. Its tangent is flat in two places, at x equals zero and at x equals three. At three, the curve turns, from falling to rising. That's the creek at the bottom of the valley. But at zero it doesn't turn. It levels off for an instant, like a flat ledge on the way down, then keeps falling. So what decides whether the curve turns?"
